    "done_when": "Read section 9 of a-worker-is-charged-to-a-job first. The refusal the sbatch and srun shims print when a launch is nested inside the fleet allocation (reckon/nested_launch.py, which names RECKON_ALLOW_NESTED_LAUNCH) says plainly that two routes remain. A separate partition job, for example on all_debug or betelgeuse, is a legitimate way to discharge heavy work. RECKON_ALLOW_NESTED_LAUNCH=1 is the explicit opt-in for submitting from inside the allocation. The compute section that reckon/crew/worker_digest.py composes into a worker's brief carries the same two routes in one sentence that the digest itself adds. The source text it digests lives outside this repository and stays untouched. tests/test_nested_refusal_names_the_route.py asserts that the refusal text and the digested compute section each name both routes, deriving the route names from the module's own constants rather than from literals. It fails at your base. Existing tests reaching nested_launch and worker_digest keep passing; grep tests/ for nested_launch, OVERRIDE_ENV and worker_digest to build the gate. Record the outcome in docs/evidence/fragments/a-worker-is-charged-to-a-job/nested-refusal-names-the-route.html. Run `date -u` first and treat that instant as your start; your deadline is 60 minutes later. Write your manifest before starting any long command. Run both gate arms with pytest-xdist (-n 8 --timeout=300), never serially. Run the base arm, from a `git archive` extraction of your base under /tmp in a directory named for this run, and then the head arm, each in the foreground: a background command dies when your turn ends. Keep the gate to the test files that reach your change, tens of files rather than hundreds. Each arm uses its own basetemp outside any repository and writes to its own new log path, which it never overwrites. Each arm is recorded as JSON carrying completed true and a literal command with absolute paths and no angle-bracket placeholder. Each log names its revision on the first line as revision= followed by the full sha, and ends with a bare line reading EXIT= followed by the exit code. The head arm adds no failure id; any added id means status blocked, naming each id. ruff check and ruff format --check over the changed Python paths report no finding the base did not. Scratch goes under /tmp in a directory named for this run and is deleted before status complete. The turn ends once the manifest reads complete or blocked.",
